  "body": "From https://github.com/mikewest/securer-contexts/issues/2.\r\n\r\nHistory is scoped to the top-level browsing context (due to Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy (COOP) it probably ought to be scoped to something higher, e.g., a currently fictional \"browsing session\"). For security purposes it would be nice if it access to it were restricted to first-party-origin documents. In other documents the API could no-op. This would probably have to use some kind of opt-in, but investigations to what extent this could be how history works, period, would be very interesting.\r\n\r\nNote that history in the HTML Standard at the moment is a work of fiction and doesn't match any implementation: #1454.\r\n\r\ncc @mikewest ",
